# Pin stable ALSA card names for the two USB audio devices.
#
# wake_word.py opens plughw:mic,0 and plughw:speaker,0 by *name*, never by
# index, because indexes move: the Pi Zero 2W has one USB port, everything hangs
# off a bus-powered hub, and the hub re-enumerates in arbitrary order after a
# replug or a brownout. This mic has been card 1 and card 2 on different boots.
#
# This file is why those names exist. It was hand-written on the Pi once and
# lived nowhere else, so the re-setup wiped it and both the wake word and the
# speaker died at the same instant with "Cannot get card index for mic" —
# 3297 crash-restarts before anyone connected the two symptoms. It is in the
# repo now, and setup.sh installs it.
#
# KERNEL=="card?*" because only the card device carries a writable id attribute;
# the sound subsystem also emits controlC0, pcmC0D0c and friends, and an
# ATTR{id} assignment on those is a silent no-op.

# C-Media / TI PCM2902 USB PnP Sound Device. Capture only; this is the mic.
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="sound", KERNEL=="card?*", ATTRS{idVendor}=="08bb", ATTRS{idProduct}=="2902", ATTR{id}="mic"

# AB13X USB headset adapter. The only USB card with a playback device, so this
# is what Desky talks out of.
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="sound", KERNEL=="card?*", ATTRS{idVendor}=="001f", ATTRS{idProduct}=="0b21", ATTR{id}="speaker"
